<section class="sec" id="details">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head reveal"><span class="ey">What it does</span><h2>Built around the supplier workflow.</h2><p class="lead">Keep the technology behind the scenes and make the outcome easy for your team to understand.</p></div>
    <div class="feature-grid"><article class="feature-card reveal"><span class="feature-card__icon">01</span><h3>Buyer authentication</h3><p>Identify the enterprise buyer and launch the correct supplier experience.</p></article><article class="feature-card reveal"><span class="feature-card__icon">02</span><h3>cXML + OCI</h3><p>Support the two procurement protocols already implemented in PunchOut Central.</p></article><article class="feature-card reveal"><span class="feature-card__icon">03</span><h3>Secure catalog sessions</h3><p>Open a buyer-specific ecommerce session without sending them through normal checkout.</p></article><article class="feature-card reveal"><span class="feature-card__icon">04</span><h3>Cart return</h3><p>Send the selected cart back to procurement for internal approval.</p></article><article class="feature-card reveal"><span class="feature-card__icon">05</span><h3>Multiple buyers</h3><p>Manage more than one enterprise customer without rebuilding the core platform.</p></article><article class="feature-card reveal"><span class="feature-card__icon">06</span><h3>Testing and go-live</h3><p>Use standard integration support to configure, test and launch the connection.</p></article></div>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="sec soft" id="workflow">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head center reveal"><span class="ey">How it works</span><h2>A simple path from buyer request to result.</h2><p class="lead">The platform keeps each step connected.</p></div>
    <div class="simple-steps"><article class="simple-step reveal"><span class="simple-step__num">01</span><h3>Buyer starts in procurement</h3><p>The buyer opens your catalog from their procurement system.</p></article><article class="simple-step reveal"><span class="simple-step__num">02</span><h3>PunchOut Central authenticates</h3><p>The request is matched to the correct buyer and store.</p></article><article class="simple-step reveal"><span class="simple-step__num">03</span><h3>Buyer shops your catalog</h3><p>They browse products and build a cart in Shopify.</p></article><article class="simple-step reveal"><span class="simple-step__num">04</span><h3>Cart returns for approval</h3><p>The cart goes back to procurement. It is not the final order yet.</p></article></div>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="sec soft" id="proof">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head reveal"><span class="ey">Built for trust</span><h2>Proven enough for the customer you cannot afford to lose.</h2><p class="lead">Simple on the surface. Dependable underneath.</p></div>
    <div class="metrics-row">
      <article class="metric reveal"><strong>90+</strong><span>customers use PunchOut technology built by our team.</span></article>
      <article class="metric reveal"><strong>$50M+</strong><span>in order value processed through our technology every year.</span></article>
      <article class="metric metric--dark reveal"><strong>cXML + OCI</strong><span>Buyer sessions, carts, POs, store orders and invoices stay connected and visible.</span></article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="sec">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head reveal"><span class="ey">Keep exploring</span><h2>Explore the platform</h2></div>
    <div class="related-grid"><a class="related-card reveal" href="/platform/purchase-orders/"><span>Platform</span><h3>Purchase Orders</h3><p>See what happens after the buyer approves the cart.</p><b>Explore &rarr;</b></a><a class="related-card reveal" href="/platform/transactions/"><span>Platform</span><h3>Transactions</h3><p>Track the full PunchOut transaction and troubleshoot issues.</p><b>Explore &rarr;</b></a><a class="related-card reveal" href="/how-it-works/"><span>Guide</span><h3>How It Works</h3><p>Follow the complete six-step order journey.</p><b>Explore &rarr;</b></a></div>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="sec soft" id="faq">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head center reveal"><span class="ey">FAQ</span><h2>Questions suppliers usually ask</h2></div>
    <div class="faq reveal"><div class="fi"><button class="fq" type="button"><span>Does cart return create the Shopify order?</span><span class="plus">+</span></button><div class="fa"><p>No. Cart return sends the selected cart back to procurement. The final ecommerce order is created after the approved PO is received.</p></div></div><div class="fi"><button class="fq" type="button"><span>Which protocols are supported?</span><span class="plus">+</span></button><div class="fa"><p>cXML and OCI are implemented.</p></div></div><div class="fi"><button class="fq" type="button"><span>Can one account support multiple enterprise buyers?</span><span class="plus">+</span></button><div class="fa"><p>Yes. PunchOut Central is designed for multiple buyer connections per account.</p></div></div></div>
  </div>
</section>
